 <th>enters+exits quickly</th>
 <th>enters</th>
 <th>exits</th>
 <th>exits+enters quickly</th>
<tr>
 <th>Firefox 51</th>
 <th>enters</th>
 <th>enters</th>
 <th>exits</th>
 <th>exits</th>
</table>

Safari 10 behaved strangely when testing in BrowserStack, seemingly hanging, so I don't trust what I saw.

[Exit fullscreen](https://fullscreen.spec.whatwg.org/#exit-fullscreen) has an early return in the spec, which makes the first two cases simple. For the last two, it's not obviously well defined, because two "resizes" are racing "in parallel."

